sentences.l:
As when winds, two, stir up the fish-teeming sea,
the North Wind and the West Wind, which two from Thrace blow,
having come suddenly;

and up stood Agamemnon,
shedding a tear, like a spring dark-watered,
which down from a sheer rock pours gloomy water;

So, I suppose, to Zeus exceeding-strong it is likely to be dear,
who indeed of many cities has undone the heads
and still will undo;

and there is great need for all the Achaeans
of good and close-packed counsel, because enemies near the ships
are burning many fires;

But when of drink and of food they had put away desire,
for them the old man, first of all, began to weave a plan,
Nestor, whose counsel earlier too appeared best;

For no other will think a better thought than this,
such as I think, both long ago and still even now,
from the time when, Zeus-sprung one, Briseis, the girl,
Achilles being incensed, you went from the hut, having taken her away,
not at all according to our mind;
